title: Conductor 0.3.1 — Wiring Fixes + The Physical Orchestration Vision
summary: Fixed 7 runtime wiring gaps in Conductor 0.3.0 that left the system structurally assembled but inert. The root cause was ownership inversion — InputOrchestrator lived as a @StateObject inside a SwiftUI view while the true lifecycle owner (AppDelegate) had no access to it. Established the single-owner architecture pattern where AppDelegate owns all stateful components and views observe them.
